---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import CtaBlock from "../components/CtaBlock.astro";
import { CHANNELS, getModules, utm } from "../lib/course";

const modules = await getModules();
const labCount = modules.filter((m) => m.data.lab).length;
---

<Base
  title="Learn | The AI Runtime"
  description="The training ground of The AI Runtime: free, practitioner-grade courses for engineers shipping AI to production. Start with Course 001, Engineering Long-Running AI Agents."
  pageSlug="home"
>
  <div class="shell">
    <section class="hero section">
      <p class="eyebrow">THE AI RUNTIME · LEARN</p>
      <h1 class="hero__title">Training for engineers who ship AI</h1>
      <p class="hero__sub">
        Free, practitioner-grade courses where you break a running system on purpose and prove
        the fix. No accounts, no paywall, no certificates: public, reproducible evidence that
        you can operate agents in production.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="courses">
      <h2>Courses</h2>

      <article class="card card--flagship">
        <div class="card__head">
          <p class="card__eyebrow">COURSE 001 · <span class="card__live">LIVE</span></p>
          <p class="card__stats">16 modules · {labCount} Failure Labs · 15-20 h · free</p>
        </div>
        <h3 class="card__title"><a href="/course-001/">Engineering Long-Running AI Agents</a></h3>
        <p class="card__promise">
          Build an agent that keeps making correct progress after the request ends, the process
          dies, a tool times out, a human disappears for three hours, and the context window
          fills up.
        </p>
        <p class="card__detail muted">
          The FDE track: one deliberately boring application, sixteen production questions,
          and a Failure Lab for every primitive. You break the system first, then earn the
          abstraction, then prove the invariant with a check anyone can run.
        </p>
        <div class="card__meta">
          <span class="card__rhythm">BUILD <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span> BREAK
            <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span> DIAGNOSE <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span> FIX
            <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span> PROVE</span>
        </div>
        <div class="card__actions">
          <a class="btn btn--solid" href="/course-001/">Start the course</a>
          <a class="btn" href="/course-001/labs/">Browse the {labCount} labs</a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <div class="card-grid">
        <article class="card">
          <p class="card__eyebrow">FIELD LAB · LIVE</p>
          <h3 class="card__title">
            <a href={CHANNELS.lab} rel="noopener">The AI Runtime Field Lab</a>
          </h3>
          <p class="card__detail muted">
            Open engineering challenges with real customer-shaped problems, a reliability bar,
            and public Field Reports. Where course skills meet unscripted work.
          </p>
          <p class="card__link">
            <a href={CHANNELS.lab} rel="noopener">lab.theairuntime.com &rarr;</a>
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <p class="card__eyebrow">PODCAST</p>
          <h3 class="card__title">
            <a href={utm(CHANNELS.podcast, "home", "listen")} rel="noopener">FDE Talks</a>
          </h3>
          <p class="card__detail muted">
            Practitioners who shipped long-running agents in production, interviewed at the
            standard this course trains: what happens after failure, with evidence.
          </p>
          <p class="card__link">
            <a href={utm(CHANNELS.podcast, "home", "listen")} rel="noopener">Listen &rarr;</a>
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card card--planned">
          <p class="card__eyebrow">COURSE 002 · IN PLANNING</p>
          <h3 class="card__title">Shaped by Course 001 graduates</h3>
          <p class="card__detail muted">
            The next course is chosen by what practitioners hit after this one. Finish the
            gauntlet, tell us where it hurt, and subscribe to vote on what gets built.
          </p>
          <p class="card__link">
            <a href={utm(CHANNELS.substack, "home", "subscribe")} rel="noopener">Subscribe to shape it &rarr;</a>
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="how">
      <h2>How these courses work</h2>
      <div class="how">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--muted">FAILURE FIRST</p>
          <p class="muted">
            You lose a run before learning checkpointing, duplicate a report before learning
            idempotency, and watch two workers collide before learning leases. The primitive
            arrives after the failure makes it necessary.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--muted">EVERYTHING REPRODUCIBLE</p>
          <p class="muted">
            Deterministic fixture servers, pinned environments, one command per lab. The
            failure you hit is the failure everyone hits, so fixes are provable rather than
            anecdotal.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--muted">EVIDENCE, NOT BADGES</p>
          <p class="muted">
            Completion means a public reliability report a stranger can re-run, not a
            certificate. The strongest reports become FDE Talks episodes.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <CtaBlock slot="footer-cta" pageSlug="home" />
</Base>

<style>
  .hero { padding-top: 4rem; }
  .hero__title { font-size: var(--t-hero); margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
  .hero__sub {
    font-size: var(--t-h3);
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    margin: 0;
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  .card {
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--bg);
    padding: 1.5rem;
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
  }
  .card--flagship {
    border-color: var(--accent-dim);
    background: var(--bg-raise);
    padding: 2rem;
  }
  .card__head {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 0.5rem 2rem;
    align-items: baseline;
  }
  .card__eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
  }
  .card__live {
    background: var(--accent);
    color: var(--bg);
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 0.1rem 0.5rem;
  }
  .card__stats {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--t-meta);
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .card__title { font-size: var(--t-h2); margin: 0 0 0.75rem; }
  .card__title a { color: var(--fg); }
  .card__title a:hover { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
  .card--flagship .card__promise {
    font-size: var(--t-body);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--fg);
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  .card__detail { font-size: var(--t-meta); max-width: var(--measure); }
  .card__meta { margin: 1rem 0; }
  .card__rhythm {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--fg);
  }
  .card__rhythm span { color: var(--accent); }
  .card__actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.75rem; margin-top: 1rem; }
  .card__link { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--t-meta); margin: 0; }
  .card--planned { border-style: dashed; }
  .card--planned .card__title { color: var(--fg-muted); font-size: var(--t-h3); }

  .card-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }
  .card-grid .card { margin: 0; }

  .how {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 2rem;
  }
  .how p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; font-size: var(--t-meta); }

  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .card-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
    .how { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
  }
</style>
